  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The direct cause of the 'B' PORV failure to stroke was determined to be a failed Stellite pilot solenoid operated valve. The steam leakage past the 'B' PORV block valve damaged the Stellite pilot SOV top stem and valve ball assembly. Additionally, Solenoid operated valves containing Stellite or Inconel were not differentiated in the material control system, leading to a Stellite SOV being released to the field for installation.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "material control / configuration management failure allowing non-conforming Stellite SOV to be installed",
    "provisional": true
